From 22a4044cee34d2d690805c753aef8567c0c61802 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 07:18:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(state): reclaim a missing turn-lease row for the matching
 holder [daveey]

Problem: Desktop session 20000101_000000_00000b called Opus successfully (325
tokens) then died as session_persistence_failed:turn_lease. The UI said another
process took over. session_turn_leases had no row; no takeover log fired.

Why 1: append_message raises SessionTurnLeaseLostError when the lease row is
missing OR the holder mismatches (hermes_state_messages.py). Evidence: two
append failures 40ms after the API success; no Interrupt requested / took over
lease line for this session.

Why 2: that single error is classified turn_lease and glossed as takeover
(hermes_state_user_copy.py). Evidence: tui turn finished cause=the takeover
copy; later read-only query found no lease row.

Why 3: expiry of a still-matching holder already renews in the same txn; a
missing row did not. Evidence: test_turn_lease_revives_expired_row vs
test_turn_lease_fences_flush_when_row_is_absent (old contract).

Root (happened): transcript writes treated a vacant lease row as takeover
instead of reclaiming it for the presented holder the way expiry revival does.

Root (not caught): tests covered mismatch-after-reclaim and expiry revival, not
matching-holder + missing row; the user copy asserted takeover from the bucket
name. Why-not-caught: no log distinguishes missing vs other-holder, so
monitors cannot tell a vacant row from a real takeover.

Recurrence: first time for this session; an earlier session_turn_lease_lost on
20000101_000000_00000c was an actual takeover interrupt.

Countermeasures:
- symptom: matching holder with no row INSERT OR IGNORE in the write txn, then
  SELECT; mismatch still refuses and names the other holder.
- detection: tests for vacant-row reclaim and mismatch-after-reclaim.
- copy: turn_lease gloss no longer claims takeover.

Proof: tests/hermes_state/test_session_turn_lease.py 28 passed with
test_storage_failure_copy and test_turn_completion_explainer.
